{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>And I will set My dwelling in your midst, and My soul shall not reject you.</b> געילה has the sense of expelling/casting out, as in (2 Samuel 1:21) ״כי שם נגעל מגן גבורים״ — it did not receive the anointing with which one anoints the skin with oil. And from this matter: ״לא מאסתים ולא געלתים״ — 'I did not reject them and did not cast them out,' meaning I did not distance them; and so Onkelos, of blessed memory, translated: ״ולא ירחיק מימרי״ — 'and My Memra shall not distance.'" "<b>And by way of</b> the Kabbalah: ״ונתתי משכני בתוככם ולא תגעל נפשי אתכם״ — נפשי said of the Holy One, blessed be He, refers to the Shekhinah. And this is what is written (Psalms 24): ״אשר לא נשא לשוא נפשו״, from what is written (Deuteronomy 5): ״לא תשא את שם ה׳ אלהיך״, and Onkelos translated לשום את שמו (ibid. 12) לאשראה שכנתיה; and this (Jeremiah 5): ״ואם בגוי אשר כזה לא תתנקם נפשי״ — for it is the attribute of judgment; and this (Judges 10): ״ותקצר נפשו בעמל ישראל״ — for the Shekhinah is distressed by the toil of Israel, and ״בכל צרתם לו צר״; and this (Jeremiah 13): ״במסתרים תבכה נפשי מפני גוה״; and the masters of truth called it בתי בראי.<br><b>And it is explicitly stated:</b> they said in the Sifrei, ״וגעלה נפשי אתכם״ — this is the withdrawal of the Shekhinah. But here, since it mentions משכני, which is the Shekhinah, one must say that when it mentions נפשי the intent is upward, to Binah, which is the soul of the attributes; for if the intent were the Shekhinah, what reason would there be to say that He will not reject us — for since She is among us, there is no need to say He will not distance us.<br><b>Rather,</b> the meaning of the verse is: ״ונתתי משכני״ — this is the Shekhinah that encompasses and draws the force of seven; ״ולא תגעל נפשי״ — concerning the soul of the attributes, that it shall receive us; for the souls have their root from there and their return is there. And therefore it explained that after it receives them, it shall not expel them — and this is a promise that we shall not need reincarnation (gilgul). And he hinted here that the entire structure is complete, for this is the promise of the time of perfection; and this shall be in the manner of what is written (Amos 6): ״נשבע אדני אלהים בנפשו״ — for the Adon in whom is mercy swears by His soul, which is the soul of the attributes; and it is as David, of blessed memory, said (Psalms 143): ״באמונתך ענני״ — which is Ḥokhmah, and it is an oath; and so Scripture states explicitly (ibid. 89): ״נשבעת לדוד באמונתך״, and this is clear."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:28:49.460440697Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}